<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating the exact diagonal length of a rectangular field with surd dimensions using Pythagoras' theorem</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A rectangular school playing field has length \({@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\text{ m}\) and width \({@b@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\text{ m}\). A straight footpath runs diagonally from one corner of the field to the opposite corner.</p>
<p>Find the exact length of the diagonal footpath, giving your answer in the form \(k\sqrt{m}\), where \(m\) has no perfect-square factors. <i>(Note: For example, write <code>15*sqrt(11)</code> to represent \(15\sqrt{11}\).)</i></p>
<p>Diagonal length = [[input:ans1]] metres [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Apply Pythagoras' theorem to the right-angled triangle formed by the length, width, and diagonal</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle d^2 = \text{length}^2 + \text{width}^2 = \left({@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\right)^2 + \left({@b@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\right)^2\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Square each term using \((k\sqrt{n})^2 = k^2 \times n\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \left({@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\right)^2 = {@a@}^2 \times \left(\sqrt{{@n@}}\right)^2 = {@a2@} \times {@n@} = {@a2n@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \left({@b@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\right)^2 = {@b@}^2 \times \left(\sqrt{{@n@}}\right)^2 = {@b2@} \times {@n@} = {@b2n@}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 3: Add the squared values and take the square root</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle d^2 = {@a2n@} + {@b2n@} = {@d2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">Since \({@d2@} = {@c2@} \times {@n@}\) and \({@c2@} = {@c@}^2\) is the largest perfect-square factor of \({@d2@}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle d = \sqrt{{@d2@}} = \sqrt{{@c2@} \times {@n@}} = \sqrt{{@c2@}} \times \sqrt{{@n@}} = {@c@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\text{ metres}\)</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Diagonal length} = {@ta1@}\text{ metres} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
